{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Fund dedicated public vape recycling bins across England",
        "additional_details": "Although retailers must already provide vape and battery recycling services, more accessible public collection points are needed to prevent litter, fires and recyclable materials going to waste. So, we are asking the Government to:\r\n1. Introduce secure vape recycling bins in town centres, shopping areas and other public spaces across England\r\n2. Work with councils and waste operators to ensure safe collection\r\n3. Explore funding from vape manufacturers and retailers to reduce costs to taxpayers",
        "background": "We want the Government to introduce a nationwide network of dedicated public vape recycling bins across England. Millions of vapes are incorrectly disposed of every week, often ending up in general or recycling bins. Due to their lithium batteries, they can catch fire, risking waste workers' safety.",
